{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Deliver this instance's unacknowledged messages to one peer, oldest first, stopping at the first failure. Fired by the peer CONNECT event (whose data carries the peer under `id`) and by send; safe to call by hand. Also the module that holds peerchat's shared helpers: the per-peer append-only chat file (runtime/peerchat/chats/<peer>.jsonl: message rows {id, me, text, time} and receipt rows {ack, time}), messages() which folds it, the unread/last state record (runtime library, peerchat_state), nudge() which fires the peerchat MESSAGE event {peer}, and deliver(). Returns OK.","import":"use ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse flowlang::appserver::fire_event;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::system::time::time;\nuse std::collections::HashSet;\nuse std::io::Write;\nuse std::path::PathBuf;\nuse std::sync::Mutex;\nuse std::sync::atomic::{AtomicUsize, Ordering};","params":[{"desc":"UUID of the peer whose pending messages should be delivered. Named id because the peer CONNECT event's data carries the peer under that key.","name":"id","type":"String"}],"returntype":"String","type":"rust"},"id":"gqwrkg1a1c7084cb7p2","readers":[],"time":1794340635268,"username":"system","writers":[]}